   "source": [
    "# Optional Lab: Gradient Descent for Climate Action\n",
    "\n",
    "<figure>\n",
    "    <center> <img src=\"https://source.unsplash.com/random/800x200/?climate\" style=\"width:800px;height:200px;\" ></center>\n",
    "</figure>\n",
    "\n",
    "**Real Impact**: Optimizing investment in renewable energy to reduce carbon emissions is one of the most critical challenges of our time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Goals\n",
    "- Implement Gradient Descent from scratch\n",
    "- Apply it to **CO₂ reduction** modeling\n",
    "- Understand learning rate effects in a high-stakes context\n",
    "- Visualize convergence and divergence"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Problem Statement\n",
    "\n",
    "| Renewable Investment ($B) | CO₂ Reduction (Million Tons) |\n",
    "|---------------------------|-------------------------------|\n",
    "| 10                        | 45                            |\n",
    "| 25                        | 120                           |\n",
    "| 40                        | 180                           |\n",
    "| 55                        | 230                           |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x_train = np.array([10, 25, 40, 55])\n",
    "y_train = np.array([45, 120, 180, 230])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Compute Cost & Gradient"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compute_cost(x, y, w, b):\n",
    "    m = x.shape[0]\n",
    "    cost = 0\n",
    "    for i in range(m):\n",
    "        f_wb = w * x[i] + b\n",
    "        cost += (f_wb - y[i])**2\n",
    "    return cost / (2 * m)\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_gradient(x, y, w, b):\n",
    "    m = x.shape[0]\n",
    "    dj_dw = 0\n",
    "    dj_db = 0\n",
    "    for i in range(m):\n",
    "        f_wb = w * x[i] + b\n",
    "        dj_dw += (f_wb - y[i]) * x[i]\n",
    "        dj_db += (f_wb - y[i])\n",
    "    return dj_dw/m, dj_db/m"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Gradient Descent Implementation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def gradient_descent(x, y, w_in, b_in, alpha, num_iters):\n",
    "    w, b = w_in, b_in\n",
    "    J_history = []\n",
    "    for i in range(num_iters):\n",
    "        dj_dw, dj_db = compute_gradient(x, y, w, b)\n",
    "        w = w - alpha * dj_dw\n",
    "        b = b - alpha * dj_db\n",
    "        J_history.append(compute_cost(x, y, w, b))\n",
    "        if i % 100 == 0:\n",
    "            print(f\"Iter {i:4d}: Cost {J_history[-1]:.2f}, w={w:.4f}, b={b:.4f}\")\n",
    "    return w, b, J_history"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Run with good learning rate\n",
    "w_final, b_final, costs = gradient_descent(x_train, y_train, 0, 0, 0.001, 2000)\n",
    "print(f\"Optimal: w={w_final:.4f}, b={b_final:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Visualizations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.plot(costs)\n",
    "plt.title('Cost Reduction Over Iterations (Climate Investment)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Iteration')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Cost')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
